Optional components downloaded at runtime
=========================================

These are not part of InkDoc's own distribution. They are downloaded only when
the user chooses to, from their official source first and from InkDoc's GitHub
mirror (byte-identical copies) as a fallback, and are verified against SHA-256
hashes pinned in InkDoc. Their license texts are installed next to them
(<engines folder>/glm-ocr/licenses/) and ship inside InkDoc in
app/core/assets/licenses/.

GLM-OCR model (GGUF build)
  Model:    zai-org/GLM-OCR          https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-OCR
  GGUF:     ggml-org/GLM-OCR-GGUF    https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/GLM-OCR-GGUF
  License:  MIT (per the model card)
  InkDoc uses the model only. It does not use the GLM-OCR SDK or the
  PP-DocLayoutV3 layout model (both Apache License 2.0).

llama.cpp (llama-server and its libraries)
  Source:   ggml-org/llama.cpp       https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
  License:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors

IBM Docling engine pack
  Source:   docling-project/docling  https://github.com/docling-project/docling
  License:  MIT (the pack bundles Docling's own dependencies under their licenses)

Bundled conversion libraries are listed with their licenses in README.md
("Authors, Credits & License").
